   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Strengthening the Power of Youth Voices (SPYV) project is a 4-year initiative targeting
adolescents, young women and young men between 15 and 35 years old, through existing organized
community-based groups. This project is being implemented by Siasa Place and Centre for Multiparty
Democracy (CMD-Kenya), with funding from the Embassy of Netherlands covering six counties in Kenya
including Busia, Homabay, Lamu, Kericho, Kitui, and Nairobi. The project is working with County
authorities (both the Executive and Assembly wings).</narrative>
   </description>
